{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"alias":"subsolar-sonorous-puppy","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batch_resume.py::test_benchmark_commit_count_is_ceil_per_pass` (integration tier, n=3000 tickets with 1 comment each) hit the 300 s pytest-timeout on 2026-11-04 on a macOS host at load average 25-33. That happened twice: once in `make verify`'s integration tier (xdist worker gw2 \"node down: Not properly terminated\"), and again when run alone.\n\nThe timeout stack was in import's comment pass: `rebar._io.import_ndjson.import_tickets` (line 290) -> `rebar._lib_mutations.comment` (line 74) -> `emit_cross_session_warning` (`src/rebar/_lib_warn.py:59`) -> `cross_session_warning_for` (`src/rebar/_commands/cross_session.py:54`) -> `show_ticket` -> `_reads._fresh` -> `ensure_fresh` (`src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py:221`), waiting on a `git` child.\n\n`ensure_fresh` spawns `git rev-parse --verify <branch>` before it checks its 60 s marker throttle, so every comment imported pays a full ticket read plus at least 1 git child process for an advisory cross-session warning. On an import of n comments that is n extra processes, and the cost scales with host load.\n\nThe comment path has existed since 2026-08-27 (`65208a7ef81`, `6d95718080c`). It was found while verifying `quartzitic-deathful-needletail`, whose change touches only `tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py`.\n\n## Next check\n\nCount the git child processes per imported comment (a Popen counter around `rebar.import_tickets` with n=50). Then compare against an import with the cross-session warning disabled, to test whether the warning read accounts for the per-comment process cost.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The git child-process count for importing n comments is measured and recorded on this ticket, with and without the cross-session warning read.\n- [ ] Importing n comments does not start a git child process per comment for the cross-session warning; verified by a test that counts Popen calls during a small import.","id":"571b-f552-5fa7-4b74","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Import comment pass starts a git process per comment for the cross-session warning"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793789358020115001,"uuid":"020e85c7-c892-4e5d-bc71-3d48a58294a5"}